Cell["\<\
ASpin = Plankette + Plankette
 as a vector in one dimition _ a pure spin _ toque is the product vector
Spin is directonless within the spins frame of reference
Can only get direction when viewed from higher frame of reference with \
additional degree of fredom
Plankette + Plankette
Rotation is binary; the Plankette is either in rotation or not in rotation
If not rotating has the value of I (?) and is undetectable. This is The \
Quatum and in effect The Universe. All else being multipul observations of \
the same Plankette.
If Rotating has the value of 2I and can be detacted based on its resultend \
torque. The torque will be the vector product of the two Planettes. Either \
can be called the real with the other  being the reflection. Model must be \
agaist a one dimitional point. Rotation can occor on the point. (can the \
rotation be across multilpule accesss, if so would be up to n -> rotation \
angles - this implies ... need to think about).



        \
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f3b1808e-8cd8-4da6-9c78-4469f99e18f5"],

